<pre class=metadata>
Title: Linked Form Controls
Shortname: linked-form-controls
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/HTML-Additions/linked-form-controls/spec/
Repository: arronei/HTML-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: This specification extends HTML with a <code>link</code> content attribute for text-entry
    <{input}> elements and for <{select}> elements. The attribute names the control that continues
    the current one. The user agent moves focus through the resulting chain of controls as each one
    fills up, and carries typing, deletion, caret movement, pasting, and autofill across the controls.
    When linked controls share a name, their values are submitted together as one form entry.
    Segmented fields such as telephone numbers and one-time codes then work without script.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css no
Complain About: accidental-2119 yes, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
</pre>

